# Crilio Decants — project rules

Canonical spec: `docs/technical-blueprint.md`.

Headless perfume decant store: **Next.js (App Router)** storefront on Vercel + **WordPress/WooCommerce** (Spaceship) via **WPGraphQL / WooGraphQL**. Checkout, Cart, and My Account stay on WooCommerce.

## Stack (do not replace without asking)

- Package manager: **bun**
- UI: **Tailwind CSS v4** + **shadcn/ui** (`radix-nova`, light-only for now)
- Data: native `fetch` GraphQL client in `src/lib/graphql` — **no Apollo/urql**
- Cart: React Context + `localStorage` hydration (when implemented)
- Payments: WooCommerce **Cash on Delivery** only on the checkout subdomain

## WordPress plugins (Spaceship)

Allow: WooCommerce, WPGraphQL, WPGraphQL WooCommerce (WooGraphQL).

**Do not install:** Headless Mode (use §6 `template_redirect` PHP), WPGraphQL CORS (use §6a whitelist PHP).

## Env

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_WORDPRESS_API_URL` — WPGraphQL endpoint
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_CHECKOUT_URL` — WooCommerce origin for cart handoff
- `REVALIDATE_SECRET` — webhook auth for `/api/revalidate` (server-only)

## Platform split

| Surface | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Homepage, catalog, PDP, cart page | Next.js |
| Checkout (COD), My Account | WooCommerce |

## Folder map

- `src/lib/graphql` — fetch client + query documents
- `src/lib/cart` — cart types + checkout handoff URL builder
- `src/context` — CartProvider (future)
- `src/components/{ui,layout,catalog,cart,product}`
- `src/app/api` — revalidate route handler (future)
- `src/types` — WooCommerce/GraphQL types
- `docs/` — technical blueprint (source of truth)

## Coding norms

- Prefer Server Components; mark `"use client"` only for interactive UI (variants, cart drawer, filters).
- Match existing shadcn / Tailwind patterns; do not invent a parallel design system.
- Keep diffs focused — no drive-by refactors or unsolicited docs.
- Commits use **Conventional Commits** (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, …). Husky runs lint-staged + `tsc` on pre-commit and commitlint on commit-msg.
- **Color contrast:** `bg-gold` buttons use `text-navy` (never white). Do not use `text-gold` on light surfaces — reserve gold for fills, borders, and icons (or brand marks on navy). Body copy uses `text-ink` / `text-navy`; `text-muted-foreground` is for captions only.
